-- lib/nbe.cub — typed codes Code(Γ, A) = Σ c. Der(Γ, c, A) over the one representation of terms
-- (lib/code.cub's Code), their evaluation, and normalization by evaluation with its soundness
-- equation (paper §6.1, (6.1) and (6.5)). Loaded after lib/std.cub.
--
-- Plan (2026-11-12). The whole construction, in the order it is built.
--
-- 0. Source of the method. Kripke normalization by evaluation for dependent types with a logical
--    relation (computability) over the category of contexts and order-preserving renamings: the
--    method of Altenkirch–Kaposi (LMCS 2017) and Coquand ("Canonicity and normalization for
--    dependent type theory", TCS 2019), and for the cubical part Sterling–Angiuli (LICS 2021).
--    The derivations are indexed by their meaning (McBride, "Outrageous but meaningful
--    coincidences", 2010): a derivation of c : A in Γ carries, as an index, the meaning of c as a
--    function of the environment. So eval is that index, the object theory's conversion is the
--    language's own judgmental equality on meanings (no conversion rule, nothing to make coherent),
--    and (6.5) holds by the indices.
--
-- 1. Objects, each defined once.
--    Raw     the existing Code (lib/code.cub); normal forms here use cvar, clam, capp, cpair, cfst,
--            csnd, ccase #0 (Bool), ccon #0 k, cplam, cpapp — the codes the language's own (code t)
--            writes for the same terms.
--    Types   (revised 2026-11-12, see the finding below) a type is a shape (TyShape, closed data)
--            with a closure: a base K, a map from the environment into K, and the shape's structure
--            over K, whose components are again closures (Clo, ElC). Its meaning ElC is computed by
--            recursion on the shape, so it is definitional at open environments; pulling a type
--            back along a map of environments (weakening, substitution) composes the map and is
--            definitional; no reindexing operation or law is needed.
--    Ctx     a context: a skeleton (list of shapes, closed data) with a closure per entry; its
--            environment type is computed by recursion on the skeleton.
--    Var, Der  variables and typing derivations, Der Γ D c v: c is a derivation-checked raw code
--            of type D in Γ with meaning v : (ρ : G) → T ρ.
--    Code Γ D = Σ c. Σ v. Der Γ D c v; eval = the meaning v (paper (6.1)).
--    Ne, Nf  neutral and normal derivations, same indices; embed : Nf → Der keeps c and v.
--    OPE     order-preserving embeddings Δ → Γ (the Kripke worlds), with actions on Var, Ne, Nf.
--    Comp D Δ δ x  the computability of x : (ρ : D) → T (δ ρ) at world Δ, by recursion on D:
--            Bool — a normal form with meaning x; Π — Kripke: at every later world, computable
--            arguments give computable results; Σ — componentwise.
--    reify/reflect  mutually by recursion on D: reify : Comp → Σ c. Nf with meaning exactly x;
--            reflect : Ne → Comp. The Π clauses are the paper's Kripke clauses (§6.1).
--    fund    the fundamental lemma, by recursion on Der: a derivation's meaning is computable at
--            every world under every computable environment.
--    normalize d = reify (fund d (reflected identity environment)); the result is a Code with the
--            same meaning index, so reifySound (6.5) is refl: eval (reify v) ρ ≡ denote v ρ.
--
-- 2. Phases. P1 the fragment Π, Σ, Bool (with dependent case): shapes and closures, Ctx, Var,
--    Der, Code, eval, Ne, Nf, embed, OPE and actions, Comp with its monotonicity (renaming)
--    law, reify/reflect, fund, normalize, reifySound. P2 PathP and the interval: worlds with
--    dimension variables and face restrictions (Comp at a path type is computability of every
--    dimension instance, with the boundary). P3 Kan operations, transp and hcomp, at Π, Σ, Bool,
--    PathP: Sterling–Angiuli's stabilization (neutrals carry the face on which they are unstable).
--    P4 Glue. P5 the specializer over Code (lib/specialize.cub's normalize, t11) — needs each
--    definition reflected into Der, which is the typed checker's output (goal typed-checker).
--    P6 universes: codes decoded by shape recursion at a fixed top level, smaller levels lifted
--    (see the correction below).
--
-- Correction (2026-11-12, replaces t45, closed): universes are not blocked and need nothing added to
-- the core. The object hierarchy U_0..U_k is finite, so it is interpreted at a fixed top meta level
-- (the Gödel stratification): one type-structure family at that level, smaller meanings lifted to
-- it. A lift is a Σ with a field at the target level filled by one fixed constant (Lift1 A = A ×
-- (Type → Type), checked); a `data ... : Type 1` annotation does not raise a level (a data type's
-- level is its fields' largest: `data Lift0 (A : Type) : Type 1 = lift0 (x : A)` is accepted but
-- `CtxL (Lift0 Unit)` at `CtxL : Type 1 → Type 2` is refused, "actual: Type (lmax lzero lzero)").
-- What lifting does not give is the round trip raise (lower x) ≡ x definitionally (the core has η
-- for Π and Σ, none for a unit type), so El (π a b) ≡ Π (El a) (El b) between a lifted code and the
-- top-level Π holds as an equivalence, not judgmentally. P6 therefore interprets each universe as
-- codes (shape and closure, as below) decoded by shape recursion, and states El's commutation with
-- the type formers as paths used by an explicit conversion rule at universe-decoded types.
--
-- Finding (2026-11-12) that fixes the design below: transport along a constant line of a variable
-- type does not reduce (CCHM has no regularity; `transport (λ i → A) a ≡ a` by refl is refused, while
-- at Bool it is accepted). The language's indexed families are forded (each index an equation field),
-- so a function defined by recursion over one computes its clauses only up to such transports when
-- the index involves variable types: `K (ty-bool G) D δ x` came out with `comp (λ i → D) [] ρ` in its
-- body. Everything whose clauses must compute inside types (the meaning of a type, computability,
-- environments of a context) is therefore defined by recursion on closed first-order skeletons
-- (TyShape, lists of shapes), where clauses compute definitionally; indexed families (derivations,
-- normal forms, renamings) are only ever the arguments of functions whose result types are fixed by
-- their signatures, so the transports inside their results are harmless (their indices, the
-- meanings, are fixed by the types).
--
-- Elaborator quirk found 2026-11-12: in a structural recursion, an implicit binder after the recursive
-- argument is not abstracted in the induction hypothesis (the inner call gets the outer value, and an
-- explicit {..} is ignored); such parameters are taken explicitly here.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- types: shapes and closures
data TyShape = s-bool | s-pi (a : TyShape) (b : TyShape) | s-sig (a : TyShape) (b : TyShape)
-- the structure of a Bool type: nothing; One1 is a type at level 1 with the one value `one`
data One1 = one1 (pad : Type → Type)
one : One1
one = one1 (λ X → X)
-- a shape's structures over a base K and their meanings
TyU : Type → Type 2
TyU K = (M : Type 1) × (M → K → Type)
-- a closure over environments K: a base K', the map into it, a structure over K'
CloU : (K : Type) → ((K' : Type) → TyU K') → Type 1
CloU K u = (K' : Type) × (K → K') × fst (u K')
ElCU : (K : Type) → (u : (K' : Type) → TyU K') → CloU K u → K → Type
ElCU K u A k = snd (u (fst A)) (snd (snd A)) (fst (snd A) k)
-- by recursion on the shape: Π and Σ have a domain closure and a codomain closure over the
-- environments extended by the domain
TyE : TyShape → (K : Type) → TyU K
TyE s-bool K = (One1 , λ D k → Bool)
TyE (s-pi a b) K =
  ((A : CloU K (TyE a)) × CloU ((k : K) × ElCU K (TyE a) A k) (TyE b) ,
   λ D k → (x : ElCU K (TyE a) (fst D) k) → ElCU ((k : K) × ElCU K (TyE a) (fst D) k) (TyE b) (snd D) (k , x))
TyE (s-sig a b) K =
  ((A : CloU K (TyE a)) × CloU ((k : K) × ElCU K (TyE a) A k) (TyE b) ,
   λ D k → (x : ElCU K (TyE a) (fst D) k) × ElCU ((k : K) × ElCU K (TyE a) (fst D) k) (TyE b) (snd D) (k , x))
-- a type of shape s over environments K, and its meaning
Clo : TyShape → Type → Type 1
Clo s K = CloU K (TyE s)
ElC : (s : TyShape) → (K : Type) → Clo s K → K → Type
ElC s K = ElCU K (TyE s)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- types over a context's environments
-- a type over environments G: a shape with a closure; its meaning; pulling back along f : H → G
PTy : Type → Type 1
PTy G = (s : TyShape) × Clo s G
ElP : (G : Type) → PTy G → G → Type
ElP G A ρ = ElC (fst A) G (snd A) ρ
pull : (G H : Type) → (H → G) → PTy G → PTy H
pull G H f A = (fst A , (fst (snd A) , (λ h → fst (snd (snd A)) (f h)) , snd (snd (snd A))))
-- Bool, and Π and Σ of a closure pair as types over G (the closures of every type former are
-- general: a Π type over G is any closure whose shape is s-pi, at any base K and map g)
bool-ty : (G : Type) → PTy G
bool-ty G = (s-bool , (Unit , (λ ρ → unit) , one))
pi-ty : (G K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : G → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k)) → PTy G
pi-ty G K a b g A B = (s-pi a b , (K , g , (A , B)))
sig-ty : (G K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : G → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k)) → PTy G
sig-ty G K a b g A B = (s-sig a b , (K , g , (A , B)))
-- the domain of such a Π (or Σ) as a type over G, and its codomain over G extended by the domain
cl-dom : (G K : Type) (a : TyShape) (g : G → K) (A : Clo a K) → PTy G
cl-dom G K a g A = pull K G g (a , A)
cl-cod : (G K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : G → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k)) →
  PTy ((ρ : G) × ElP G (cl-dom G K a g A) ρ)
cl-cod G K a b g A B = pull ((k : K) × ElC a K A k) ((ρ : G) × ElP G (cl-dom G K a g A) ρ) (λ p → (g (fst p) , snd p)) (b , B)
-- the meanings are the language's own Π and Σ (definitionally)
pi-meaning : (G K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : G → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k)) (ρ : G) →
  Path Type (ElP G (pi-ty G K a b g A B) ρ) ((x : ElP G (cl-dom G K a g A) ρ) → ElP ((ρ : G) × ElP G (cl-dom G K a g A) ρ) (cl-cod G K a b g A B) (ρ , x))
pi-meaning G K a b g A B ρ = refl

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- contexts
-- a context over a skeleton (its entries' shapes, closed data): the entries' closures and the type of
-- its environments, by recursion on the skeleton
CtxU : Type 2
CtxU = (M : Type 1) × (M → Type)
CtxE : Lst TyShape → CtxU
CtxE lnil = (One1 , λ γ → Unit)
CtxE (lcons s sk) =
  ((γ : fst (CtxE sk)) × Clo s (snd (CtxE sk) γ) ,
   λ p → (ρ : snd (CtxE sk) (fst p)) × ElC s (snd (CtxE sk) (fst p)) (snd p) ρ)
Ctx : Type 1
Ctx = (sk : Lst TyShape) × fst (CtxE sk)
Env : Ctx → Type
Env Γ = snd (CtxE (fst Γ)) (snd Γ)
emp : Ctx
emp = (lnil , one)
-- Γ extended by a type over its environments
ext : (Γ : Ctx) → PTy (Env Γ) → Ctx
ext Γ A = (lcons (fst A) (fst Γ) , (snd Γ , snd A))
ext-env : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) → Path Type (Env (ext Γ A)) ((ρ : Env Γ) × ElP (Env Γ) A ρ)
ext-env Γ A = refl

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- variables
-- the dependent eliminator of Bool, for the meanings of case
bool-elim : (P : Bool → Type) → P true → P false → (b : Bool) → P b
bool-elim P t f true = t
bool-elim P t f false = f
-- the four parts every judgment here is indexed by: a context, a type over its environments, a raw
-- code and the code's meaning (the indices are one Σ: a family's indices may not depend on each other)
Jdg : Type 1
Jdg = (Γ : Ctx) × (A : PTy (Env Γ)) × Code × ((ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ)
-- the variable n of Γ (its code cvar n), of type A, meaning v (a projection out of the environment)
wk : (Γ : Ctx) (B : PTy (Env Γ)) → PTy (Env Γ) → PTy (Env (ext Γ B))
wk Γ B A = pull (Env Γ) (Env (ext Γ B)) (λ ρ → fst ρ) A
data Var : (J : Jdg) → Type 1 where
  vz : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) → Var (ext Γ A , wk Γ A A , cvar #0 , λ ρ → snd ρ)
  vs : (Γ : Ctx) (A B : PTy (Env Γ)) (n : Word) (v : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ) →
       Var (Γ , A , cvar n , v) → Var (ext Γ B , wk Γ B A , cvar (%wsucc n) , λ ρ → v (fst ρ))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- neutral and normal forms
-- one family for both (mutual data types are not available), the kind in the index. η-long: a
-- neutral is normal only at Bool. The codes are the ones the language's (code t) writes: Bool is
-- data #0, true and false its constructors #0 and #1, case on it ccase #0 with the two branches.
data NK = k-ne | k-nf
-- substituting a meaning for the last variable, and extending at the case's scrutinee
at-last : (G : Type) (A : PTy G) (va : (ρ : G) → ElP G A ρ) → PTy ((ρ : G) × ElP G A ρ) → PTy G
at-last G A va B = pull ((ρ : G) × ElP G A ρ) G (λ ρ → (ρ , va ρ)) B
c-true : Code
c-true = ccon #0 #0 lnil lnil
c-false : Code
c-false = ccon #0 #1 lnil lnil
c-case : Code → Code → Code → Code
c-case t f x = ccase #0 (lcons t (lcons f lnil)) x
data NN : (KJ : NK × Jdg) → Type 1 where
  nvar : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) (n : Word) (v : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ) →
    Var (Γ , A , cvar n , v) → NN (k-ne , (Γ , A , cvar n , v))
  napp : (Γ : Ctx) (K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : Env Γ → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k))
    (f : Code) (vf : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (pi-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B) ρ)
    (c : Code) (va : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) ρ) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ , pi-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B , f , vf)) → NN (k-nf , (Γ , cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A , c , va)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) va (cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B) , capp f c , λ ρ → vf ρ (va ρ)))
  nfst : (Γ : Ctx) (K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : Env Γ → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k))
    (p : Code) (vp : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (sig-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B) ρ) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ , sig-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B , p , vp)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ , cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A , cfst p , λ ρ → fst (vp ρ)))
  nsnd : (Γ : Ctx) (K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : Env Γ → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k))
    (p : Code) (vp : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (sig-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B) ρ) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ , sig-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B , p , vp)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) (λ ρ → fst (vp ρ)) (cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B) , csnd p , λ ρ → snd (vp ρ)))
  ncase : (Γ : Ctx) (P : PTy (Env (ext Γ (bool-ty (Env Γ))))) (x : Code) (vx : (ρ : Env Γ) → Bool)
    (t : Code) (vt : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (at-last (Env Γ) (bool-ty (Env Γ)) (λ ρ → true) P) ρ)
    (f : Code) (vf : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (at-last (Env Γ) (bool-ty (Env Γ)) (λ ρ → false) P) ρ) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ , bool-ty (Env Γ) , x , vx)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (bool-ty (Env Γ)) (λ ρ → true) P , t , vt)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (bool-ty (Env Γ)) (λ ρ → false) P , f , vf)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (bool-ty (Env Γ)) vx P , c-case t f x ,
                λ ρ → bool-elim (λ b → ElP (Env (ext Γ (bool-ty (Env Γ)))) P (ρ , b)) (vt ρ) (vf ρ) (vx ρ)))
  nne : (Γ : Ctx) (x : Code) (vx : (ρ : Env Γ) → Bool) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ , bool-ty (Env Γ) , x , vx)) → NN (k-nf , (Γ , bool-ty (Env Γ) , x , vx))
  ntrue : (Γ : Ctx) → NN (k-nf , (Γ , bool-ty (Env Γ) , c-true , λ ρ → true))
  nfalse : (Γ : Ctx) → NN (k-nf , (Γ , bool-ty (Env Γ) , c-false , λ ρ → false))
  nlam : (Γ : Ctx) (K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : Env Γ → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k))
    (c : Code) (vb : (ρ : Env (ext Γ (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A))) → ElP (Env (ext Γ (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A))) (cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B) ρ) →
    NN (k-nf , (ext Γ (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) , cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B , c , vb)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ , pi-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B , clam c , λ ρ x → vb (ρ , x)))
  npair : (Γ : Ctx) (K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : Env Γ → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k))
    (c1 : Code) (v1 : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) ρ)
    (c2 : Code) (v2 : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (at-last (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) v1 (cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B)) ρ) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ , cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A , c1 , v1)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) v1 (cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B) , c2 , v2)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ , sig-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B , cpair c1 c2 , λ ρ → (v1 ρ , v2 ρ)))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- typing derivations, typed codes
-- Der (Γ , A , c , v): c is a code of type A in Γ with meaning v. The object theory's conversion is
-- the language's judgmental equality of meanings, so there is no conversion rule: a β-redex's
-- meaning is already its contractum's.
data Der : (J : Jdg) → Type 1 where
  dvar : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) (n : Word) (v : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ) →
    Var (Γ , A , cvar n , v) → Der ((Γ , A , cvar n , v))
  dapp : (Γ : Ctx) (K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : Env Γ → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k))
    (f : Code) (vf : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (pi-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B) ρ)
    (c : Code) (va : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) ρ) →
    Der ((Γ , pi-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B , f , vf)) → Der ((Γ , cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A , c , va)) →
    Der ((Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) va (cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B) , capp f c , λ ρ → vf ρ (va ρ)))
  dfst : (Γ : Ctx) (K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : Env Γ → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k))
    (p : Code) (vp : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (sig-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B) ρ) →
    Der ((Γ , sig-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B , p , vp)) →
    Der ((Γ , cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A , cfst p , λ ρ → fst (vp ρ)))
  dsnd : (Γ : Ctx) (K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : Env Γ → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k))
    (p : Code) (vp : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (sig-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B) ρ) →
    Der ((Γ , sig-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B , p , vp)) →
    Der ((Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) (λ ρ → fst (vp ρ)) (cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B) , csnd p , λ ρ → snd (vp ρ)))
  dcase : (Γ : Ctx) (P : PTy (Env (ext Γ (bool-ty (Env Γ))))) (x : Code) (vx : (ρ : Env Γ) → Bool)
    (t : Code) (vt : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (at-last (Env Γ) (bool-ty (Env Γ)) (λ ρ → true) P) ρ)
    (f : Code) (vf : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (at-last (Env Γ) (bool-ty (Env Γ)) (λ ρ → false) P) ρ) →
    Der ((Γ , bool-ty (Env Γ) , x , vx)) →
    Der ((Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (bool-ty (Env Γ)) (λ ρ → true) P , t , vt)) →
    Der ((Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (bool-ty (Env Γ)) (λ ρ → false) P , f , vf)) →
    Der ((Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (bool-ty (Env Γ)) vx P , c-case t f x ,
                λ ρ → bool-elim (λ b → ElP (Env (ext Γ (bool-ty (Env Γ)))) P (ρ , b)) (vt ρ) (vf ρ) (vx ρ)))
  dtrue : (Γ : Ctx) → Der ((Γ , bool-ty (Env Γ) , c-true , λ ρ → true))
  dfalse : (Γ : Ctx) → Der ((Γ , bool-ty (Env Γ) , c-false , λ ρ → false))
  dlam : (Γ : Ctx) (K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : Env Γ → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k))
    (c : Code) (vb : (ρ : Env (ext Γ (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A))) → ElP (Env (ext Γ (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A))) (cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B) ρ) →
    Der ((ext Γ (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) , cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B , c , vb)) →
    Der ((Γ , pi-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B , clam c , λ ρ x → vb (ρ , x)))
  dpair : (Γ : Ctx) (K : Type) (a b : TyShape) (g : Env Γ → K) (A : Clo a K) (B : Clo b ((k : K) × ElC a K A k))
    (c1 : Code) (v1 : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) ρ)
    (c2 : Code) (v2 : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (at-last (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) v1 (cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B)) ρ) →
    Der ((Γ , cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A , c1 , v1)) →
    Der ((Γ , at-last (Env Γ) (cl-dom (Env Γ) K a g A) v1 (cl-cod (Env Γ) K a b g A B) , c2 , v2)) →
    Der ((Γ , sig-ty (Env Γ) K a b g A B , cpair c1 c2 , λ ρ → (v1 ρ , v2 ρ)))
-- typed codes (paper §6.1): Code(Γ, A) = Σ c. Der(Γ, c, A), the meaning carried with the derivation
TCode : (Γ : Ctx) → PTy (Env Γ) → Type 1
TCode Γ A = (c : Code) × (v : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ) × Der (Γ , A , c , v)
-- evaluation (6.1): eval_{Γ,A} : Code(Γ, A) → Π ρ : Env(Γ). ⟦A⟧ρ
teval : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) → TCode Γ A → (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ
teval Γ A t = fst (snd t)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- worlds: order-preserving embeddings
-- OPE (Δ , Γ , r): Δ is Γ with entries inserted; r is its meaning, the map of environments
OIx : Type 1
OIx = (Δ : Ctx) × (Γ : Ctx) × (Env Δ → Env Γ)
data OPE : (W : OIx) → Type 1 where
  -- (the empty context's structure is any value of One1, which has no η)
  odone : (γ : One1) → OPE ((lnil , γ) , (lnil , γ) , λ ρ → ρ)
  odrop : (Δ Γ : Ctx) (r : Env Δ → Env Γ) (B : PTy (Env Δ)) → OPE (Δ , Γ , r) → OPE (ext Δ B , Γ , λ ρ → r (fst ρ))
  okeep : (Δ Γ : Ctx) (r : Env Δ → Env Γ) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) →
    OPE (Δ , Γ , r) → OPE (ext Δ (pull (Env Γ) (Env Δ) r A) , ext Γ A , λ p → (r (fst p) , snd p))
-- the identity world, by recursion on the skeleton
oid : (sk : Lst TyShape) (γ : fst (CtxE sk)) → OPE ((sk , γ) , (sk , γ) , λ ρ → ρ)
oid lnil γ = odone γ
oid (lcons s sk) γ = okeep (sk , fst γ) (sk , fst γ) (λ ρ → ρ) (s , snd γ) (oid sk (fst γ))
